    "body": "## Summary\n- Add a `CUDNN_FRONTEND_GIT_REF` build arg to `docker/Dockerfile.fw_final`, pinned to the tip of `NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend` branch `feat/1.29.0-megatron`.\n- The ref is installed over the PyPI wheel after the environment sync, before the base-runtime check. `fw_final` re-syncs with `fw_pyproject.toml` (pins `nvidia-cudnn-frontend==1.29.0`), so an install made earlier in `Dockerfile.ci` would be replaced.\n- Skipped when the arg is empty or `PRESERVE_BASE_RUNTIME=True`.\n- Docker-only: no change to `pyproject.toml`, `fw_pyproject.toml` or `uv.lock`. The Bridge CI image (`Dockerfile.ci`) is unchanged and keeps the locked wheel.\n\n## Not yet verified\n- Test image build (draft until done).\n- That the branch's distribution name and version match `nvidia-cudnn-frontend` 1.29.0 or higher (`gdn_utils.py` expects at least 1.29.0).\n- That the image has git and build tools for the native build.\n\n## Docs and tests\nREADME build-arg table for `Dockerfile.fw_final` updated. No Python changes, so no unit tests added.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
